as handed."}, {"turn": 15, "text": "Opus 5.5 answered with G5 instead of the engine's E2, and the lead went from +4.6 to -3.8, an 8.3 point loss. The offered edge was gone in a single move, and E2 was left for White to take at move 26."}, {"turn": 17, "text": "G4 lost 9.5 points, taking Black from -3.8 to -13.3, and it was Opus 5.5's worst move. The engine wanted F7, and White took F7 next, building the upper-centre group. Black's stones on the right were now a wall facing nothing much."}, {"turn": 25, "text": "H6 lost another 5.2 points, from -14.5 to -19.7, with the engine preferring C7. The game was already well behind, and this pushed it near -20."}, {"turn": 40, "text": "By the end White had D3, E3, C3 and B3 across the third line, with E1 and F1 on the bottom edge. Black's last stones at D2, F2 and G1 sat at -22.4, and Opus 5.5 resigned."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only parses a pasted board and prints each group's stones and liberties, and the other commands just read notes (cat/tail games.md) and append game logs to games.md and CLAUDE.md; nothing ranks moves or looks ahead.", "stop": false}}